§ `Điều 18.1 — partial loss`

-- A bumper replaced new for 20,000,000 on a 37-month car: 15% (not for business) leaves
-- 17,000,000; 20% (for business) leaves 16,000,000. A repaired door is not depreciated.
#ASSERT `art 18.1 — the reasonable cost of` `a new bumper costing 20 million` `with` 37 `months of use, for business` FALSE `, depreciating` TRUE EQUALS 17_000_000
#ASSERT `art 18.1 — the reasonable cost of` `a new bumper costing 20 million` `with` 37 `months of use, for business` TRUE `, depreciating` TRUE EQUALS 16_000_000
#ASSERT `art 18.1 — the reasonable cost of` `a door repaired for 5 million` `with` 37 `months of use, for business` FALSE `, depreciating` TRUE EQUALS 5_000_000
#ASSERT `art 18.1 — the reasonable cost of` `a new bumper costing 20 million` `with` 37 `months of use, for business` FALSE `, depreciating` FALSE EQUALS 20_000_000
-- The traction battery at 37 months, not for business: 30% off 300,000,000 = 210,000,000.
#ASSERT `art 18.1 — the reasonable cost of` `a new traction battery costing 300 million` `with` 37 `months of use, for business` FALSE `, depreciating` TRUE EQUALS 210_000_000
-- A tyre (18.1.2(c)): 30% in the first year, 50% after.
#ASSERT `art 18.1.2 — the depreciation rate for` `a new tyre costing 4 million` `with` 12 `months of use, for business` FALSE EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT `art 18.1.2 — the depreciation rate for` `a new tyre costing 4 million` `with` 13 `months of use, for business` FALSE EQUALS 50%
-- A part replaced new 6 months before, with documents, is aged 6 months, not 100.
#ASSERT `art 18.1.2 — the depreciation rate for` `a new tyre costing 4 million, the old one fitted new 6 months ago` `with` 100 `months of use, for business` FALSE EQUALS 30%
#ASSERT `art 18.1.2 — the depreciation rate for` `a new bumper costing 20 million, the old one fitted new 6 months ago` `with` 100 `months of use, for business` FALSE EQUALS 0%
#ASSERT `art 18.1.2 — the depreciation rate for` `a new bumper costing 20 million` `with` 100 `months of use, for business` FALSE EQUALS 25%
-- 18.1.3: repainting the whole car only above 50% of the paint.
#ASSERT `art 18.1.3 — the repainting payable` `bumper and door damage, 51% of the paint` EQUALS 30_000_000
#ASSERT `art 18.1.3 — the repainting payable` `bumper and door damage, 50% of the paint` EQUALS 0
-- 18.1.2(a): insured for 400 of 500 million: ratio 0.8.
#ASSERT `art 18.1.2(a) — the ratio for under-insurance` `cover of 400 million on a car worth 500 million` EQUALS 0.8
#ASSERT `art 18.1.2(a) — the ratio for under-insurance` `cover of 600 million on a car worth 500 million` EQUALS 1
-- The partial loss before the deductible: 17,000,000 + 5,000,000 = 22,000,000; under-insured,
-- x 0.8 = 17,600,000; with no depreciation, 25,000,000.
#ASSERT `art 18.1 — the partial loss before the deductible` `cover of 500 million at full value` `bumper and door damage` 37 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 22_000_000
#ASSERT `art 18.1 — the partial loss before the deductible` `cover of 400 million on a car worth 500 million` `bumper and door damage` 37 FALSE TRUE EQUALS 17_600_000
#ASSERT `art 18.1 — the partial loss before the deductible` `cover of 500 million at full value` `bumper and door damage` 37 FALSE FALSE EQUALS 25_000_000

§ `Điều 18.2-18.3 — total loss and salvage`

-- 340 of 450 million is 75.6%: both limbs. 337.5 is exactly 75%: the first limb (more than 75%)
-- fails and the second (75% or more) holds. 337 is 74.9%: neither.
#ASSERT `art 18.2.1 — a total loss by damage` `damage costing 340 million to repair, the car worth 450 million`
#ASSERT `art 18.2.1 — a total loss by damage` `damage costing 337.5 million to repair, the car worth 450 million`
#ASSERT NOT `art 18.2.1 — damaged by more than 75% of the market value` `damage costing 337.5 million to repair, the car worth 450 million`
#ASSERT NOT `art 18.2.1 — a total loss by damage` `damage costing 337 million to repair, the car worth 450 million`
-- 18.2.3: the market value at the loss, at most the sum insured.
#ASSERT `art 18.2.3 — the total loss payable` `cover of 500 million at full value` `damage costing 340 million to repair, the car worth 450 million` EQUALS 450_000_000
#ASSERT `art 18.2.3 — the total loss payable` `cover of 400 million on a car worth 500 million` `damage costing 340 million to repair, the car worth 450 million` EQUALS 400_000_000
#ASSERT `art 18.3.2 — the deduction where the owner keeps the wreck` `a total loss, the owner keeping the wreck worth 50 million` EQUALS 50_000_000
#ASSERT `art 18.3.2 — the deduction where the owner keeps the wreck` `damage costing 340 million to repair, the car worth 450 million` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT NOT `art 18.2.2 — a stolen vehicle may be paid as a total loss` `bumper and door damage`

§ `Điều 19 — the deductible`

-- 500,000 against 500,000: nothing; 500,001: 1.
#ASSERT `art 19.2 — the loss after the deductible` 500_000 500_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `art 19.2 — the loss after the deductible` 500_001 500_000 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `art 19.3 — the deductible per loss` `cover of 500 million at full value` EQUALS 500_000
#ASSERT `art 19.3 — the deductible per loss` `cover with a deductible of 10 million` EQUALS 10_000_000
